For a reversible adiabatic expansion of an ideal gas:

\[
T_2 = T_1\left(\frac{V_1}{V_2}\right)^{\gamma-1}
\]

Argon is monatomic, so \(\gamma = 5/3\) and \(\gamma - 1 = 2/3\).

\[
T_2 = 273.15\left(\frac{1.0}{3.0}\right)^{2/3}
= 273.15 \times 3^{-2/3}
\approx 131\ \text{K}
\]

Final answer: (H)

