Combine potentials by electron-weighted average:

\[
E^\circ_{\mathrm{Ce^{4+}/Ce}}
=\frac{(1)E^\circ_{\mathrm{Ce^{4+}/Ce^{3+}}}+(3)E^\circ_{\mathrm{Ce^{3+}/Ce}}}{4}
\]

Using \(E^\circ_{\mathrm{Ce^{4+}/Ce^{3+}}}\approx 1.61\text{ V}\) and \(E^\circ_{\mathrm{Ce^{3+}/Ce}}\approx -2.34\text{ V}\):

\[
E^\circ=\frac{1.61+3(-2.34)}{4}\approx -1.34\text{ V}
\]

Final answer: H

